WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.560
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.520
<i>Hoshikawa Hisui has been 
searching for a book,</i>

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.570
<i>a diary penned by his deceased mother.</i>

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.240
<i>When the girl learns that 
Shiginuma Shouko has the diary,</i>

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.720
<i>she heads to Nachtigal with Hisui.</i>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.760
<i>As Hisui holds the diary,</i>

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.990
<i>he's embraced by the warm, 
gentle aura of his mother's love.</i>

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.830
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her separation.</i>

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:10.110
The identity of the drowned body found in 
Shinobazu Pond is that of Baron Ikari Tadashi,

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.940
a member of the House of Peers.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.720
Fukurou was also notified, as there was 
a Japanese-style book found near the body.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.160
A cursed tome.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.680
Nabari-kun is investigating 
it in the laboratory now.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.660
This is the fourth victim.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:31.420
All four are House members who agreed with 
Prime Minister Ukai's disarmament policy.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.420
Does that mean people who oppose 
disarmament are behind this?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.110
Many on the opposing side hail from 
the military or industrial groups.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:44.680
Their leader is one deeply involved in the 
munitions business: Shiginuma Takashi-san.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.010
He's got to be behind Karasu—

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.570
We still don't have proof.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.930
Essentially, in order to derail 
the disarmament policy,

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.440
Karasu is going after Ukai's 
supporters with cursed tomes.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.440
Killing them off and making 
it look like suicide.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.420
I don't think they'll stop at 
House of Peers members.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.950
Their ultimate goal is the 
Prime Minister himself.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.960
Movie Theater After the Rain

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.960
-Tears-

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
My wallet and handkerchief...

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.970
Yep, I have everything.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.720
All set.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.970
Good morning, Kuze-sama.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.450
Good morning.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.540
Y-You're awfully dressed up.
Are you going somewhere?

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.240
Yes.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.940
I have very important business.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.000
Flower Theater

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.500
<b>Back Alley Boys</b>

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.750
I'm totally serious!

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.360
This movie is really good.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.520
Is it?

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.580
Next time you're off duty, 
you should go see it.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.150
But neither Hitaki nor Gramps can go with me.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.160
Well, then, what about someone 
from your apartment?

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:29.190
No way! I couldn't go to 
a movie alone with a boy!

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.910
Besides, they're all busy with work, too.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.670
I didn't say you had to go 
with just one of them...

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.280
I guess you could just 
see it by yourself, then.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.180
This is the Taisho Era.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.440
There's nothing embarrassing about
a lady seeing a movie by herself!

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.050
Yeah, the movie really—Oh!

00:04:58.720 --> 00:04:59.640
My apologies.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:00.540
It's fine.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.840
I'm sorry.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:03.610
Kuze?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.070
Akira?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.050
Are you here to see this, too?

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.510
I'm off duty.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:14.860
R-Right.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.460
Are you here as a couple?

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.670
A couple? No, we're not!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.460
Would you like to be admitted as a couple?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.450
One male.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.970
And one female.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:31.720
Currently, the male and female 
seating areas are both full.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.620
Would you like to enter as a couple?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.390
A couple, then.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:40.480
Certainly, sir.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.520
Wasn't that a great movie?

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.780
Huh? Yeah.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.390
Especially that last scene.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.270
It was so moving, it brought me to tears.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:27.150
It was.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:30.480
So you're actually the crying type, Akira?

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.160
I was pretty surprised.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.410
I'm hopeless with that stuff.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:39.830
I get emotionally invested easily, 
so when I see that kind of thing, I just...

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.590
Just wipe it completely from your mind.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:46.670
Sure.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.950
It's starting to rain.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.060
Don't worry about me.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.680
No, get under here.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.940
I said no.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.660
You can be surprisingly 
stubborn, despite your looks.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:05.940
Just get under here.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:08.820
So we're going to share 
an umbrella, like lovers?

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.570
But the rain...

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.520
Young master, this way.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:42.990
How's that?

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.520
Just splendid!

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.980
Good morning.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.290
Good morning.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.520
Morning.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.820
Going out somewhere?

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.530
The Prime Minister's residence.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:08:00.160
Shougo-kun, let me know if you'd like me 
to pass anything along to your father.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.170
There's nothing.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.430
All right, then.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.370
Let's go, Kuze.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:09.780
Yes. We'll be off, then, Shougo.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.050
O-Okay...

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:19.530
Understood.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:22.440
I will tell the House members to be mindful

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.500
of unfamiliar Japanese-style books.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.060
Please be careful yourself, 
as well, Prime Minister.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.880
I know.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:32.820
Have you found any proof linking 
Karasu to the cursed tomes?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.660
Unfortunately not.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.560
The police commissioner just reported

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.570
that they were able to get an 
investigator inside Nachtigal.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.790
To try and find proof linking 
Shiginuma and Karasu?

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.460
Yes.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.960
By the way, he hasn't been 
giving you any trouble, has he?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.120
Shougo-kun, you mean?

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.680
What do you think, Kuze?

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:52.970
Huh? Ah... yes, ma'am!

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.010
W-Well...

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.140
There were some difficulties at first,

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:00.570
but lately he's been listening 
to his music quietly

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.980
and diligently attending 
to his cleaning duties.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:09.230
He also helped me make the beef stew 
we had for dinner the other evening.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.990
He's very good at peeling potatoes.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.000
Shougo was peeling potatoes?

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.770
Oh, p-pardon me!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.900
If I recall, you are the daughter of
Viscount Kuze Masataka, correct?

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:26.920
Yes.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.250
Thank you for telling me all that.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:31.530
Please continue looking after him.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.510
Curse that Ukai.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.520
While the major world powers 
move to expand their militaries,

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.020
he's neglecting national defense.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.520
Are you listening to me?!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.300
Measures have been taken.

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:54.400
Check.

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:05.870
The queen is mine.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.550
Please have a seat, my lady.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:21.930
Huh?

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.880
I'll get straight to the point.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.020
I want you to join me.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.440
What do you mean?

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.200
Karasu...

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:44.440
Don't be ridiculous!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.210
I need you.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.460
Why me?

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:58.470
Because you have been chosen.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:04.680
You can see things that 
ordinary people cannot.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.720
I can see the future,

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:11.230
and I will guide this country to it.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:13.230
That's insane...

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.520
No matter what you do, it's hopeless.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.990
Even if you increase security 
around the Prime Minister

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.560
or sneak some police dog 
into my organization.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.370
How do you know about that?!

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:28.620
There's a crow lurking in the owl's nest.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:33.990
I could just take you with me now,

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:37.020
but I want to respect your free will.

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:38.380
I won't go with you!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.240
If you don't come to me,

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:44.890
I can't be certain of what may happen 
to those most precious to you.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:20.710
Tokimiya-san isn't here.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.470
Akira...

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:27.220
She went to the police department. 
She won't be back until later.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:28.460
I see...

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.790
Is something wrong?

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.940
No, it's nothing.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:35.600
Hey, Kuze.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.240
Do you... want to go to the movies again?

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:46.790
Yes, I'd like that.

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:01.420
There's a crow lurking in the owl's nest.

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:10.010
It's Hoshikawa. Is this a good time?

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.270
What's going on?

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.190
We're having curry!

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.530
Shizuru-san and the others 
are making it for us.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:26.070
If you mix the curry powder with the 
remaining heat of the frying pan like this,

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.740
it won't burn.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:28.800
I see.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.040
Shougo-kun, we have more 
than enough potatoes.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.040
No!

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.610
We need more!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.840
It's amazing.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.790
I just felt like making it.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:41.800
Time to eat!

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:46.050
Delicious!

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.050
It really is very good.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.160
I am honored, my princess.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.460
Yeah, the potatoes I peeled 
are especially good!

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.840
I think there are a bit too many, though.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.060
Th-There are not!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.770
Curry should have shallots.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.630
You just don't get it, Akira.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:03.590
According to the Ukai family cooks,

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:05.190
I don't care what anyone says. 
Curry should have shallots.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.970
tonkatsu is actually a 
uniquely Japanese dish.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.830
You're going to turn into 
shallot if that's all you eat.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.570
Originally, the côtelette of 
French cuisine became the cutlet,

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:08.950
I wouldn't mind.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:09.570
What?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:13.830
and it then became modern tonkatsu 
when it was fried in oil instead of baked.

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:21.300
It's fun getting to eat with everyone.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.340
It is.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:27.240
I'm really glad I came to Fukurou.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.340
Everyone is so nice.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:33.960
After what happened with Hitaki 
and my starting to work here,

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:36.350
everyone helped me 
despite my inexperience.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:43.500
I feel truly blessed to have been
able to meet everyone here.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.740
Is that so? I'm glad, then.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:53.240
<i>There's a crow lurking in the owl's nest.</i>

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:58.370
Kuze, are you okay?

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:03.600
I'm sorry!

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:04.710
Goodness.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:06.680
I'll clean it up right away.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.380
Ouch!

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.920
This won't do.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.760
Hey, what are you trying to pull?

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.320
I have to heal the princess's wound.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:23.520
Nevertheless, it's disgraceful to try 
and put a lady's finger in your mouth!

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.520
Good grief, Shizuru-san.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.040
You're so naïve.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.070
I'll go get the emergency medical kit.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.070
I'm what?!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.440
That's Shizuru-san for you.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.840
You okay, Akira?

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:40.850
I never would've expected him 
to be squeamish about blood.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:43.330
Everyone has things they can't handle.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.830
There, that should do it.

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:52.020
Thanks.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:08.110
Ohbayashi Bookstore

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:08.110
Good afternoon.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.490
Ah, Kuze-san.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.720
Has there been anything today?

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:16.210
I haven't had any Japanese-style 
books brought in today.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:18.710
I'll just check to make sure, okay?

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:20.140
Sure, go ahead.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.020
<i>Am I being watched?!</i>

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.960
Tsugumi-chan!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.360
So, did you see the movie?

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.220
Yes.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.090
Wasn't it great?

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:55.430
It was.

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:58.030
Did something happen?

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.910
No, nothing.

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:02.450
Really?

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.670
You can tell me if something's wrong, okay?

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.470
Thanks.

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:09.380
Well, I'm going this way.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.920
Okay, see you later.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.840
Koruri-chan!

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.520
Are you all right?

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.810
It just came flying at me...

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:29.560
Is everything okay?

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:30.320
An accident?

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:32.390
Call the police!

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:45.720
<i>I can't be certain of what may happen 
to those most precious to you.</i>

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:49.830
<i>Kuze residence.</i>

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:50.960
Gramps!

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.440
<i>Oh, Tsugumi-sama!</i>

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.040
Is Hitaki doing all right?

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:59.840
<i>Yes, he seemed to enjoy the
pancakes I cooked for him today.</i>

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.400
Oh, good...

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.480
<i>Is something the matter?</i>

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.780
No, it's nothing.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:30.920
You're late.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.510
Um... I'm back.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.620
Did something happen?

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.450
I'm fine. It's nothing.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.670
I've got to keep it together.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:20.420
Kuze, are you okay?

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.330
I'm sorry! It's nothing!

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:27.060
Kuze!

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.310
Wait, Kuze!

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:33.560
I swear it's nothing!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:35.320
Was it Shiginuma?

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.570
"A crow in the owl's nest..."

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:49.830
But that can't be true. 
Everyone here is so nice.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:53.550
They can't be in Karasu...

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:57.340
What else did he tell you?

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:01.470
He told me to join Karasu or else...

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:05.600
everyone dear to me would be in danger!

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.600
Just today, Koruri-chan was almost killed!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:13.730
At this rate, Hitaki could be 
next, or everyone in Fukurou!

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.100
Calm down, Kuze!

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:18.480
What should I do, Akira?

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:21.100
I'm putting everyone at risk 
if I don't go to Karasu.

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:23.490
But someone from Karasu is in Fukurou...

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:25.660
No, that can't be true!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:30.660
All the people here are so kind... 
But the crow feathers just keep...

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:37.750
Akira?

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:45.920
Damn it, you're way too trusting.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:53.020
It's me.

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.420
Akira?

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.780
A crow feather?

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:05.280
I'm with Karasu.

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:11.300
Akira?

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:15.670
I will protect you.

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:22.360
<i>This is Kougami Akira.</i>

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:36.430
Chapter 8:  "The Colors of the Flames of Love -Tragedy-"

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:26.500
<i>I put you in a terrible situation by 
keeping my true identity a secret.</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:28.490
<i>I am truly sorry for that.</i>

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.590
<i>I swear I will protect you.</i>

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:35.500
<i>That's all I can do now.</i>

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:38.750
<i>Also, please forget our 
plans to see the movie.</i>
